    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the number of different possible starting lineups for Coach Grunt, we need to calculate the number of ways to choose the remaining 3 players out of the remaining 10 players (12 - 2 total players).\n\nThe formula for combinations is:\n\nC(n, r) = n! / [r!(n-r)!]\n\nwhere n is the total number of items to choose from, r is the number of items to choose, and ! denotes the factorial of a number.\n\nIn this case, n = 10 (remaining players) and r = 3 (remaining players to choose).\n\nSo, the number of ways to choose the remaining 3 players is:\n\nC(10, 3) = 10! / [3!(10-3)!]\n                = 10! / [3!7!]\n                = (10 × 9 × 8) / [3 × 2 × 1]\n                = 720 / 6\n                = 120\n\nTherefore, there are 120 different possible starting lineups for the Grunters.\n\n(120)",
